(text "NOTES - CONNECTION VIA BLUETOOTH / WIRELESS OPTION (rev W0.1). See ../README.md\n1. No wire between goggles and jacket. Link = ESP32-S3 radio on both ends: ESP-NOW (recommended, no pairing, low latency)\n   or Bluetooth LE. Jacket ESP32-S3-DevKitC-1 already has the radio; goggle XIAO RP2040 is replaced by a XIAO ESP32S3.\n2. XIAO ESP32S3 uses the same 14-pin XIAO layout. Same OLED pins as the cable version: D0 CS_L, D1 CS_R, D2 DC, D3 RST,\n   D8 SCK, D10 MOSI. D6/D7 (UART) no longer needed. Fit the included U.FL antenna and keep it clear of metal/carbon.\n3. Goggle power: 1S LiPo -> J5 -> SW1 -> VBAT -> TP1/TP2 -> short wires to the XIAO underside BAT+/BAT- pads.\n   The XIAO charges the LiPo from its USB-C. Battery cannot charge while SW1 is OFF.\n   CHECK LiPo connector polarity before plugging in - JST-PH battery leads are not standardised.\n4. Battery monitor: VBAT/2 via R1/R2 (220k/220k, ~9.5 uA) to D5 (GPIO6, ADC1). C1 100 nF filter.\n5. Jacket ESP32 GPIO4/5 (old cable UART) now unused. Jacket still USB powered (battery stage still open, see docs).\n6. Same unverified items as the cable version: header spacings and module pinouts must be measured before ordering." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 228.6 124.46 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "3e73dd75-fbf5-4ad8-953d-5e3f5a4d040d"))
(sheet_instances (path "/" (page "1")))
